{
  "skillId": "order-operations-indices",
  "atomType": "R",
  "theory": {
    "intro": "Powers take their place in the agreed order of operations: they are worked out **after** brackets but **before** multiplication and division.",
    "facts": [
      "The order is **brackets**, then **indices**, then $\\times$ and $\\div$ (left to right), then $+$ and $-$ (left to right).",
      "In $2\\times 5^{2}$ the power goes first: $2\\times 25=50$, not $10^{2}$.",
      "A power outside a bracket waits for the bracket: $(4+2)^{2}=6^{2}=36$.",
      "$3(9-5)^{2}$ means $3\\times(9-5)^{2}$, so the bracket, then the square, then the multiplication.",
      "A fraction bar groups the whole numerator and the whole denominator, like a pair of brackets."
    ],
    "steps": [
      "Work out anything inside brackets.",
      "Evaluate the powers.",
      "Do all $\\times$ and $\\div$ from left to right.",
      "Do all $+$ and $-$ from left to right."
    ]
  },
